summary:
  A rebuild that skips a member whose sink is not registered (LBMISS) goes
  back to leaving that member's previous loopback loaded, so the speaker is
  fed twice once the retry seats the new one.

history:
  Found 2026-09-05 reading the loopback build shell. The existence gate is
  right — loading a loopback for a sink that is not there attaches it to
  the default sink and feeds the combine into itself — but the member's OLD
  loopback from the previous build was left standing in the else branch:
  it kept feeding a sink that was not there, WirePlumber moved it onto
  whatever was, and the retry then seated a second loopback beside it.
  From 2026-09-06 the branch unloads the old module. This mutant leaves it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
                    + (oldId !== "" ? " pactl unload-module " + oldId + " 2>/dev/null;" : "") + " fi; ";

replace:
                    + (oldId !== "" ? " true " + oldId + " 2>/dev/null;" : "") + " fi; ";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_syncengine.qml
  test_a_missing_sink_takes_its_old_loopback_down_with_it. Line-neutral.
